\title{[A7] Fits (3 pts)}
\date{2026-11-19T03:09:27Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\tag{problem}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{Suppose that instead of powers of two, we represent integers as a sum of distinct Fibonacci numbers. In other words, instead of an array of bits, we keep an array of \em{fits} (\em{fi}bonacci dig\em{its}), where each fit is either 0 or 1, and the #{i^{th}} least significant fit indicates whether the sum includes the #{i^{th}} Fibonacci number #{F_{i}}. For example, the fit-string #{101110_{F}} represents the number ##{F_6+F_4+F_3+F_2=8+3+2+1=14.} Design and analyze an algorithm to increment a fit-string in #{\Theta(1)} amortized time, assuming that a fit-string counter starts at #{0} and is repeatedly incremented. As with the example above, assume that #{F_{1}=F_{2}=1}, that the array of fits is indexed starting from #{1}, and that the #{i^{th}} index of the array stores the #{i^{th}} fit. Also observe that unlike binary, a given number #{n} does not necessarily have a unique representation as a fit-string; it does not matter which representations are generated by your algorithm.}

